// Margin notes: in an aligned derivation, whatever follows `&&` on a row is the reason, not a step. Tag it so CSS can
// set it apart (dashed chalk rule, accent colour, smaller); the first note of a block gets the "why" label.
// Fit each display block in its column: shrink its math down to 86%, then put each reason under its step.
function stackNotes(t){ // "&&\htmlClass{mnote}{reason}" -> the reason on its own row under the step (brace-matched)
